      "node_type": "concept",
      "canonical_name": "Three-Phase Aspirant Motivation Cycle",
      "aliases": [
        "aspirant motivation cycle",
        "three phases of competitive prep",
        "honeymoon dip panic curve"
      ],
      "domain": "General",
      "definition": "A temporal trajectory of motivation in multi-year competitive exam preparation characterized by an initial high-motivation honeymoon phase (Days 1–90), an unmotivated psychological distance dip with high backlog accumulation (Days 90–210), and an acute anxious panic phase leading up to the examination deadline (Day 210 onwards).",
